ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":130,"prev":132,"next":135,"titles":137,"firmware":27},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":28,"procedures":95,"parameters":105,"related":106,"body":113,"sources":114,"official_url":32,"controls":127},"instrument.lfo","LFO page and LFO types (M4)",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"lfo","low frequency oscillator","modulation","lfo type","modulation source","M4 page","instrument",40,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/lfo.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[11],[17],"M4","`M4` holds one LFO per track in five types — duck, element, random, tremolo and value. `shift + M4` changes the type; most types share one layout: source or speed, amount, destination page, parameter.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[23,24,25],"1.0.15","1.1.0","1.1.3","1.1.15","1.1.33",[29,35,39,42,45,48,51,56,60,65,68,71,74,79,83,87,92],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"types","`shift + M4` switches the LFO type between duck, element, random, tremolo and value.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#lfo",null,"official",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":38,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"five-not-four","Duck arrived in OS 1.1.0; the guide's sentence listing the LFO types still counts four and leaves it out.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"layout","In element, random and value, `E1` sets the source or speed, `E2` the amount, `E3` the destination page and `E4` the parameter on that page; duck and tremolo use their own layouts.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"target","The destination is one of the track's module pages and the parameter is one of that page's four encoders; `E4` can be turned or clicked to choose it.",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"sub-functions","Extra settings sit behind encoder clicks or `shift` plus a turn; on some types a click on `E1` changes the waveform shape.",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"speed","Speed controls are tempo-synced over their anti-clockwise range; turned clockwise until a dial icon appears, they run at a free rate.",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":54,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"speed-screen","On screen a synced speed reads as a count beside a note value, 8 with a 64th at the fast end, then 6 with a 16th, 4 with a quarter and 2 with a whole note as it counts down to 1; from the middle of its range a clock dial shows the free rate.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#24-lfo-instrument-m4-five-types","verified",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":59,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"synced-rates","Synced, the speed doubles every eighth of the lane: in the middle of the synced range one cycle lasts a quarter note, anticlockwise an eighth, a 16th, a 32nd and a 64th, clockwise a half note, a whole note and a breve (two bars).","docs/research/60-sound-session.md#4-lfos",{"id":61,"text":62,"source":63,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":64},"synced-steps","The synced speed has eight steps, each double the last, and the card counts them from 8 (a 64th, fastest) down to 1 (a breve, slowest), with 5 an eighth, 4 a quarter, 3 a half and 2 a whole note; a new LFO starts on 4, a quarter note. Past 1 the dial turns to the free rate (one video, OS 1.1.x; OS 1.0's cards read differently and are not decoded).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":66,"text":67,"source":59,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"free-rates","Free, the LFO stands still at the dial's first position and speeds up ever faster, to about 21.5 cycles a second at the end.",{"id":69,"text":70,"source":59,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"amount-centre","Amount ladders are centred on zero (CC 64 over MIDI); either side of it sets the same depth with the modulation inverted.",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":59,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"cutoff-depth","Aimed at a filter's cutoff, value and random sweep its whole range at full amount; half the amount from a middle cutoff already reaches both ends.",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":77,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":33,"confidence":78},"negative","The amount can go below zero to invert the modulation; OS 1.1.3 fixed how negative amounts are drawn.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.3","derived",{"id":80,"text":81,"source":82,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"drum-reset","On drum tracks the LFO restarts with every new note.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.15",{"id":84,"text":85,"source":86,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"midi-ccs","Over MIDI, CC40–43 on the track's channel drive the four `M4` encoders in order, in all five LFO types.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#3-midi-reach-on-1133-verified-on-screen",{"id":88,"text":89,"source":90,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":91},"no-type-cc","No MIDI CC is known for the LFO type.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#33-instrument-tracks-18-synth-drum-sampler-multisampler-engines","community-verified",{"id":93,"text":94,"source":54,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":55},"off","With the LFO off, the page is dimmed under an off box; pressing `M4` again switches the LFO on.",[96],{"id":97,"goal":98,"preconditions":99,"steps":102,"result":33,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"type","Change the LFO type of the selected track",[100,101],"instrument mode","the track is selected",[103],{"keys":104,"note":33,"set":33},"shift + M4",[],[107,108,109,110,111,112],"instrument.lfo-duck","instrument.lfo-element","instrument.lfo-random","instrument.lfo-tremolo","instrument.lfo-value","sequencer.parameter-locks","An LFO rides a knob for you. Choose what drives the movement — a repeating wave (value), random steps\n(random), the unit's motion, microphone or envelope (element), another track's rhythm (duck) — then\naim it at an encoder on the track's pages. Tremolo skips the aiming: it is wired to pitch and volume.",[115,117,119,121,122,123,124,125,126],{"url":32,"kind":116},"guide",{"url":38,"kind":118},"changelog",{"url":54,"kind":120},"research",{"url":59,"kind":120},{"url":63,"kind":120},{"url":77,"kind":118},{"url":82,"kind":118},{"url":86,"kind":120},{"url":90,"kind":120},[128,129],"key.shift","key.m4",{"id":11,"title":131},"Instrument",{"id":133,"title":134},"instrument.track-sends","Track sends to aux out, tape, FX I and FX II (M3 + shift)",{"id":107,"title":136},"Duck LFO (sidechain pumping)",{"basics.key-notation":138,"basics.main-modes":139,"basics.modules":140,"basics.track-buttons":141,"basics.linked-tracks":142,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":143,"basics.workflow":144,"basics.firmware-versions":145,"hardware.layout":146,"hardware.power-and-charging":147,"hardware.connectors":148,"hardware.specifications":149,"hardware.te-boot":150,"hardware.firmware-update":151,"hardware.factory-reset":152,"hardware.system-menu":153,"hardware.safety-and-care":154,"hardware.in-the-box":155,"sequencer.overview":156,"sequencer.step-entry":157,"sequencer.step-recording":158,"sequencer.live-recording":159,"sequencer.extend-notes":160,"sequencer.nudge":161,"sequencer.single-sound":162,"sequencer.rotate":163,"sequencer.copy-step":164,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":165,"sequencer.parameter-locks":166,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":167,"sequencer.step-components":168,"sequencer.step-component-reference":169,"sequencer.component-pulse":170,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":171,"sequencer.component-multiply":172,"sequencer.component-velocity":173,"sequencer.component-ramp-up":174,"sequencer.component-ramp-dow